  "dish": {
    "id": "chocolate-makhana-mousse",
    "name": "Chocolate makhana mousse",
    "meal": "Snack",
    "minutes": 10,
    "protein": 5,
    "how": "No cooking",
    "tools": "Blender (mixie), small bowls, sieve, cling film, fridge",
    "serves": 2,
    "cover": "cover",
    "ingredients": [
      {
        "q": "~1 cup (~25 g)",
        "n": "Roasted makhana (fox nuts)",
        "tag": "makhana",
        "img": "i-makhana"
      },
      {
        "q": "~1/2 cup (120 ml)",
        "n": "Milk",
        "tag": "milk",
        "img": "i-milk"
      },
      {
        "q": "~4, soaked in the milk",
        "n": "Dates (khajoor)",
        "tag": "dates",
        "img": "i-milk"
      },
      {
        "q": "~3 tbsp (extra for dusting)",
        "n": "Cocoa powder",
        "tag": "cocoa",
        "img": "i-cocoa"
      },
      {
        "q": "a pinch",
        "n": "Cinnamon powder (dalchini)",
        "tag": "cinnamon",
        "img": "i-cinnamon",
        "opt": true
      },
      {
        "q": "~1 tbsp",
        "n": "Sliced almonds (badam)",
        "tag": "almonds",
        "img": "i-almond",
        "opt": true
      }
    ],
    "steps": [
      {
        "t": "Grind the roasted makhana to a fine powder.",
        "imgs": [
          "s-grind-1",
          "s-grind-2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "t": "Put the makhana powder in the blender jar.",
        "imgs": [
          "s-jar-1",
          "s-jar-2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "t": "Pour in the milk with the soaked dates.",
        "imgs": [
          "s-milk-1",
          "s-milk-2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "t": "Add the cocoa powder.",
        "imgs": [
          "s-cocoa-1",
          "s-cocoa-2",
          "s-cocoa-3"
        ]
      },
      {
        "t": "Add a pinch of cinnamon powder.",
        "imgs": [
          "s-cin-1",
          "s-cin-2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "t": "Blend until thick and smooth.",
        "imgs": [
          "s-blend-1"
        ]
      },
      {
        "t": "Pour the mousse into small bowls.",
        "imgs": [
          "s-pour-1",
          "s-pour-2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "t": "Top with sliced almonds.",
        "imgs": [
          "s-almond-1",
          "s-almond-2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "t": "Dust cocoa powder on top through a sieve.",
        "imgs": [
          "s-dust-1",
          "s-dust-2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "t": "Cover the bowls with cling film and chill in the fridge about 5 hours.",
        "imgs": [
          "s-chill-1",
          "s-chill-2",
          "s-chill-3"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "tags": [
      "blender"
    ],
    "notes": "Hindi voiceover is badly garbled and there is no ingredient text: ingredients identified by sight. The pinch of reddish-brown powder is probably cinnamon but could be jaggery powder. Dark bits in the milk look like dates (maybe raisins). The chill time (about 5 hours) is my best reading of the voiceover. All amounts are guesses. The grinding of makhana and the blending are not shown (only the powder and the jar pour); the first 14 seconds are an intro of the creator eating it. A fridge shelf with eggs is visible in the chill shots only as background (cropped out)."
  },
